                <pb facs="1035" n="915" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg915"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2689: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-11T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 11,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>218. Legation’s 365 of September 8, 5 p.m. Immediately after the Washington
                    Conference China was invited in a most friendly manner to consider the problem
                    of the Chinese Eastern, but she seemed to show no disposition toward
                    international cooperation. At your discretion you may point this out to the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs, referring to our telegrams 22 of February 3, 7
                        p.m.,<anchor n="87" xml:id="d747-f1"/> and 52 of March 7, 4 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="88" xml:id="d747-f2"/> and to the Legation’s telegrams 89 of March
                        8,<anchor n="89" xml:id="d747-f3"/> and 118 of March 25, 1 p.m.<anchor
                        n="90" xml:id="d747-f4"/> The other Powers are interchanging views at
                    present. In due time communication will be made to the Chinese Government.</p>
                <p>The Embassy in Japan has doubtless advised you regarding the nature of the
                    proposed action. When answers have been received from France and Italy you will
                    be completely informed. Concurrence has already been received from the British
                    and Japanese Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
